Subject: Route __settimezone through zsys_settimeofday
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted

settimeofday(NULL, tz) (glibc's __settimezone) still made the settimeofday
syscall with inline asm, which Fil-C refuses at run time ("cannot handle
inline asm ... syscall"). systemd PID 1 calls it from
clock_reset_timewarp() right after switch-root, so a Fil-C NixOS died
there. The runtime's zsys_settimeofday already checks and passes a
timezone pointer. The regression check is tests/glibc-settimezone.nix.

--- a/sysdeps/unix/sysv/linux/settimezone.c	2026-11-05 01:14:11.973431632 +0100
+++ b/sysdeps/unix/sysv/linux/settimezone.c	2026-11-05 01:14:11.984831023 +0100
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 #include <sys/time.h>
 #include <stddef.h>
 #include <sysdep.h>
+#include <pizlonated_syscalls.h>
 
 /* Set the system-wide timezone.
    This call is restricted to the super-user.
@@ -28,10 +29,5 @@
 int
 __settimezone (const struct timezone *tz)
 {
-#ifdef __NR_settimeofday
-  return INLINE_SYSCALL_CALL (settimeofday, NULL, tz);
-#else
-  __set_errno (ENOSYS);
-  return -1;
-#endif
+  return zsys_settimeofday (NULL, tz);
 }
